    <p class="sg-body">Approvals and payments have, traditionally, <b>had no defense mechanism at all</b> as a domain. For transfers and approvals, Lemma requires <b>a mathematical proof of authorization</b> and stops anything out of scope before it executes.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="sub" style="margin-top:24px">Layer a proof gate over the attacks, and the outcome changes like this:</p>
  <div class="eq">
    <div class="box atk"><div class="ic">⚠️</div><div class="t">Attack</div><div class="cap">Escalates keys/credentials and abuses them</div><ul><li>JWT privilege escalation</li><li>Impersonation</li><li>Audit-log tampering</li></ul></div>
    <div class="op">→</div>
    <div class="box add"><div class="ic">🛡</div><div class="t">Lemma’s proof gate</div><div class="cap">Demands a “proof” before execution</div><ul><li><b>Who</b> ZK identity</li><li><b>With what authority</b> role</li><li><b>On which data</b> scope</li></ul></div>
    <div class="op">→</div>
    <div class="box res"><div class="ic">🛑</div><div class="t">Stops before execution</div><div class="cap">No proof, nothing is sent</div><ul><li>fail-closed</li><li>Zero leakage</li><li>Verifiable trail</li></ul></div>
  </div>

  
